@startuml 01-component
' =====================================================================
' Automated Code Feedback -- Component Architecture
' Traces to: NFR-3, NFR-4, NFR-11, FR-37, FR-38, FR-39
'
' Key structural fact: the AI grading component runs INSIDE the
' platform autograder script, in both immediate and nightly mode. The
' nightly job runner only triggers reruns. It does not generate
' feedback.
' =====================================================================

title Component Architecture

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam ArrowColor #444444
skinparam InterfaceBackgroundColor #FFFFFF

legend top right
  |= Colour |= Owner |= Stream |
  |<#D6E4F0>| Student A | AI grading and LLM orchestration |
  |<#DCEFD9>| Student B | Web app, DB schema, repository layer |
  |<#FBE6D4>| Student C | Platform integration, autograder script |
  |<#EDE0F0>| Student D | Requirements, tests, CI/CD, docs |
  |<#E8E8E8>| -- | External, not built by us |
endlegend

actor Instructor as instr
actor Student as stud

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------
' Our cloud service
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------
package "Cloud-hosted Service (NFR-1)" {

  package "Instructor Web Application" #DCEFD9 {
    [Web Frontend] as fe #DCEFD9
    [Web Backend / REST API] as be #DCEFD9
  }

  package "Shared Data Layer" #DCEFD9 {
    [Repository Layer] as repo #DCEFD9
    database "Grading Database" as db #DCEFD9
  }
}

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------
' Inside the LMS autograder container -- NOT our infrastructure
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------
cloud "Gradescope (or other LMS)" as gs #E8E8E8 {

  [Submission UI] as gs_ui #E8E8E8
  [Feedback / Results View] as gs_fb #E8E8E8
  [Submission view\n(Rerun Autograder)] as gs_rerun #E8E8E8

  package "Autograder Container" as agbox #E8E8E8 {
    [Autograder Entrypoint] as ag #FBE6D4
    [Functional Test Runner\n(JUnit, pytest, ...)] as junit #FBE6D4
    [results.json Packager] as packager #FBE6D4
    [AI Grading Component] as aigrade #D6E4F0
  }
}

cloud "LLM Providers" as llms #E8E8E8 {
  [Anthropic API] as p_claude #E8E8E8
  [OpenAI API] as p_openai #E8E8E8
  [Google Gemini API] as p_gemini #E8E8E8
}

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------
' Nightly trigger -- thin by design
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------
package "Repository / CI-CD" #EDE0F0 {
  [Nightly Trigger Job\n(Playwright / Selenium)] as trigger #FBE6D4
  [Scheduled Workflow\n(cron)] as cron #EDE0F0
  [CI Workflow\n(on commit)] as ci #EDE0F0
  [Test Suite] as tests #EDE0F0
  [Instructor + Technical Docs] as docs #EDE0F0
}

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------
' Published interfaces -- THE CONTRACTS
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------
interface "IGradingRepository" as IRepo
interface "ILearningPlatform" as IPlat
interface "ILLMProvider" as ILLM
interface "IGradingClient" as IClient

repo -up- IRepo
trigger -up- IPlat
aigrade -up- ILLM
be -up- IClient

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------
' Wiring
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------
instr --> fe : configures targets, rubrics,\ngrading mode, reviews quality
fe --> be : HTTPS / JSON
be ..> IRepo
repo --> db : SQL

stud --> gs_ui : submits code
ag --> junit : run functional tests
ag --> aigrade : invoke in immediate mode, or on\nrerun when the submission is\nnot already AI-graded
ag --> packager
packager --> gs_fb : results.json
gs_fb --> stud : feedback

aigrade ..> IClient : HTTPS.\nread rubric + marks,\nwrite feedback + scores
aigrade ..> ILLM
p_claude <-- aigrade
p_openai <-- aigrade
p_gemini <-- aigrade

cron --> trigger : nightly
trigger --> gs_rerun : login, click\n"Rerun Autograder"\nper submission needing AI
gs_rerun --> agbox : re-runs the container

ci --> tests
tests ..> be
tests ..> aigrade
tests ..> trigger

note bottom of agbox #FFF8DC
  **OQ-11, open: where do credentials live?**
  This container is Gradescope's infrastructure,
  not ours.

  (a) Container holds the LLM API key and talks
      to the DB directly. Simplest code. Means
      every adopting instructor pastes their own
      API key into Gradescope's autograder
      settings, visible to any TA with access.

  (b) Container holds only a per-assignment
      token and calls IGradingClient, which does
      the LLM work on our side. Keys stay on our
      infrastructure. Needs a synchronous
      generate-feedback endpoint.

  Recommend (b) for an OER. The diagram shows
  (b). Switching to (a) is local to this package.
end note

note right of trigger #FFF8DC
  Deliberately thin: log in, then click Rerun
  Autograder once per submission that still has
  PENDING tasks. It does NOT call an LLM and
  does NOT write feedback. Everything else
  happens inside the container.
end note

note right of repo
  Student B owns the schema and migrations.
  A, C and D go through the repository layer
  or the REST API, never raw SQL.
end note

@enduml
